<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    MVVM (Model - View - ViewModel): the ViewModels, in pure .NET (net10.0, without WPF, checked by a test).
    - A ViewModel is the STATE of the screen (what is typed, selected, displayed, in progress) and its COMMANDS.
    - It does not know the view: it SIGNALS when a property changes (INotifyPropertyChanged), and the view, bound
      to it by data bindings, updates itself.
    - Hence the great benefit: the whole behaviour of the screen is tested without a screen, and two different views
      (Ui.Wpf and Ui.Console) plug into the same ViewModels.
    INotifyPropertyChanged, INotifyDataErrorInfo, ICommand and ObservableCollection are part of .NET itself.
  -->

